# Playwright Conventions

## Auth

Stored session by default; UI login only for login-page tests.

- `tests/auth.setup.ts` logs in once and writes `playwright/.auth/user.json`.
- Chromium specs use that `storageState` (see `playwright.config.ts` setup → chromium dependency).
- Do not call `login()` in every spec unless the test is about the login flow or auth setup is skipped.
- Credentials: `DIDAXIS_EMAIL`, `DIDAXIS_PASSWORD`, `DIDAXIS_URL` from `.env`.

## Page Objects

Follow `.cursor/skills/pom-conventions/SKILL.md`.

- One POM per page or component under `pages/`; tests import and instantiate with `new XxxPage(page)`.
- Locators: readonly constructor fields; priority `getByRole` → `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` → `getByText` → `getByTestId` (comment if needed).
- Action methods only; all `expect(...)` in specs. No `waitForTimeout` in POMs.

## Locators

Role- and label-based; never CSS or XPath; avoid brittle exact text when a role+name works.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
page.locator('.btn-primary').click();
page.getByText('Save').first().click();

// ✅ GOOD
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Save' }).click();
page.getByLabel('Program name').fill(name);
```

Disambiguate duplicates with `.filter({ hasText })`, not `.first()`.

## Data & cleanup

Follow `.cursor/skills/api-cleanup/SKILL.md`.

- Unique names: append `Date.now()` (or similar) so parallel runs do not collide.
- Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` when a test creates programs; call `trackProgram(uuid)` after `POST /api/programs` returns **201** (`data.id`).
- Teardown is API `DELETE`, not UI; never delete data the test did not create.
